[0;38;2;108;112;134mAuthor:[0;38;2;205;214;244m Stefan Haller <stefan@haller-berlin.de>[0m
[0;38;2;108;112;134mDate:[0;38;2;205;214;244m   Mon Jul 27 18:36:09 2026 +0200[0m
[0;38;2;205;214;244m[0m
[0;38;2;205;214;244m    Rework the custom pager config (rename to diff renderer)[0m
[0;38;2;205;214;244m    [0m
[0;38;2;205;214;244m    For a long time lazygit has used the term "custom pager" to refer to[0m
[0;38;2;205;214;244m    what's really a "diff renderer". A pager is a program that allows you to[0m
[0;38;2;205;214;244m    view output page by page (hence the name), e.g. less; lazygit's custom[0m
[0;38;2;205;214;244m    diff renderers are not pagers. It used the term only because the feature[0m
[0;38;2;205;214;244m    is implemented using git's GIT_PAGER env var, but that's an[0m
[0;38;2;205;214;244m    implementation detail.[0m
[0;38;2;205;214;244m    [0m
[0;38;2;205;214;244m    Rename the 'git.pagers' config to 'git.diffRenderers', and restructure[0m
[0;38;2;205;214;244m    its elements while we're at it to make things clearer:[0m
[0;38;2;205;214;244m    [0m
[0;38;2;205;214;244m    - Add a 'type' field to explicitly specify which type of diff renderer[0m
[0;38;2;205;214;244m      it is (the two fundamentally different ones are 'stdinFilter' and[0m
[0;38;2;205;214;244m      'extDiff').[0m
[0;38;2;205;214;244m    - Add a third type, 'rawGit', which has an 'args' field that makes it[0m
[0;38;2;205;214;244m      easy to use 'git --color-words' as a custom renderer[0m
[0;38;2;205;214;244m    - Unify the old 'pager' and 'externalDiffCommand' fields to a single[0m
[0;38;2;205;214;244m      'command' field for both types[0m
[0;38;2;205;214;244m    [0m
[0;38;2;205;214;244m    Existing config files are migrated automatically.[0m
[0;38;2;205;214;244m[0m

